  id: Tibialis_cranial_muscle.R
  partName: Tibialis_cranial_muscle.R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The tibialis cranialis flexes the hock joint and plays an important role in
    controlling paw placement. It ensures precise and coordinated movement during
    locomotion. '
  - This muscle helps lift the limb and position it correctly, reducing the risk
    of injury. It works with other muscles to maintain balance and stability. Its
    function is essential for smooth gait patterns and controlled movement of the
    hindlimb.
